### Status (v0.1.2 / v0.2 corrections)

**Fixed during v0.1.1/v0.1.2:**

1. ~~`application/run_bundle_impl.rs` imports `commands::run` types~~ — `application/run_bundle.rs` now owns `RunBundleRequest`/`RunResult`; `commands/run.rs` imports from the application layer (correct direction).
2. ~~`commands/pack.rs` calls `integrity`/`signing` directly~~ — the pack sequence (stage → encrypt secrets → checksum → manifest → canonical-JSON sign → validate) lives in `application/pack_bundle.rs`; `commands/pack.rs` delegates.
3. ~~Vestigial `application/init_bundle.rs`~~ — deleted (was uncompiled dead code referencing a nonexistent `Application` type).
4. ~~Bundle-root `launch` placeholder script~~ — no longer created by `pn init` (v0.1.2); launching is defined by `manifest.launch` only.

**Fixed during v0.2 (single live Harness contract):**

1. ~~Two parallel abstractions (`harness/types.rs` `HarnessAdapter` + `harness/traits.rs` `Harness`)~~ — `types.rs` deleted; one contract in `harness/traits.rs` (detect/discover/prepare_runtime) implemented by `harness/pi/harness.rs` and the aider scaffold.
2. ~~`application/pack_bundle.rs` hardcodes Pi paths / exclusion lists / packages structure~~ — pack now consumes `PortableEnvironment` from the registry; Pi vocabulary lives in `PiHarness::discover()`.
3. ~~`application/run_bundle_impl.rs` branches on `harness.name == "pi"` for the Node.js check~~ — runtime preflight goes through registry `prepare_runtime()`.
4. ~~`commands/init.rs` / `commands/pack.rs` detect via `PiInstallation` directly~~ — detection resolves through the `HarnessRegistry`; `PiInstallation` is internal to `harness/pi/`.
5. ~~`commands/diff.rs` re-implemented the Pi detection ladder (`PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` → `~/.pi/agent` → …)~~ — `pn diff` resolves the harness installation through the registry's `detect()`; the Pi env-var ladder lives in `harness/pi/` only.
6. ~~Old aider path-oriented scaffolding (`harness/aider/paths.rs`, `launch.rs` — `AiderPaths`, `build_launch_command`)~~ — deleted; aider keeps a single detection-only `harness.rs` on the `Harness` contract.

**Remaining deviations (deferred beyond v0.2):**

1. **`commands/init.rs`** still does orchestration at the command layer (directory scaffolding, manifest write) — there is no application-layer `init` use case yet.
2. **`commands/pack.rs`** still owns `--archive`/`--encrypt-archive` creation (tar.gz + passphrase prompt) after the application-layer pack succeeds.
3. **`commands/info.rs`, `commands/unlock.rs`, `commands/rekey.rs`** read manifests and touch crypto/domain directly instead of going through application-layer use cases.

---

### Target Architecture

```
CLI → Commands → Application → Domain
                          ↓
              ┌───────────┼───────────┐
              ▼           ▼           ▼
           Harness   Infrastructure  Security
```

All dependencies flow **downward** (CLI → Commands → Application → Domain/Infra/Sec/Harness).
No upward or circular dependencies. As shipped in v0.2, the `Harness` contract is
live and Pi is migrated behind it (`detect`/`discover`/`prepare_runtime` exercised
end-to-end by `init`/`pack`/`run`/`diff`); the aider detection scaffold implements
the same trait. Future work: application-layer `init`/`info`/`unlock`/`rekey` use
cases so commands become pure adapters, and wiring a second harness end-to-end.
